diff --git a/docs/examples.md b/docs/examples.md
index 2393decf..98029722 100644
--- a/docs/examples.md
+++ b/docs/examples.md
@@ -497,6 +497,27 @@ This behavior can be changed using the *on_setattr* argument.
 
 Check out {ref}`converters` for more details.
 
+## Running Custom Code Before/After Setting Attributes
+
+An `on_setattr` hook can be a generator function that yields exactly once.
+Code before the `yield` runs before the attribute is set, the yielded value is what gets stored, and code after the `yield` runs once the new value is in place.
+
+```{doctest}
+>>> def gen_hook(instance, attrib, value):
+...     print(f"got {value!r}")
+...     yield int(value) * 2 + 286
+...     print("set x to 420")
+>>> @define
+... class C:
+...     x: int = field(on_setattr=gen_hook)
+>>> c = C(42)
+>>> c.x = "67"
+got '67'
+set x to 420
+>>> c.x
+420
+```
+
 (metadata)=
 
